IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcsc-dates`
IMPORT `hcsc-core`

-- Health and Community Services Complaints Act 2004 (SA) -- THE SEAT OF THE PERSON COMPLAINING: the consumer of a
-- health or community service (the patient, the client, the resident), or the person complaining for them (a parent, an
-- attorney, a substitute decision-maker, a family member after a death). Every question is asked as that person would
-- ask it, from facts that person can state; the Commissioner's judgments are asked as conditions. The rules are in
-- hcsc-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act's current
-- version, 4.12.2025, and the Regulations' current version, 18.3.2019, as the register's unauthorised RTFs). State of
-- South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The questions of the person complaining`

§§ `Can I complain`

@export Is the service I want to complain about a health service or a community service under the South Australian Health and Community Services Complaints Act 2004 (s 4, Regulations reg 4)?
GIVEN `the kind of service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc What the service was: a service to benefit or promote health; care or accommodation premises for aged or disabled people; diagnostic or screening; ambulance; treating or preventing illness, injury, disease or disability; a service by a health professional (a registered practitioner, an audiologist, optical dispenser, dietitian, psychotherapist, social worker, counsellor, radiographer, pathology provider, anyone whose occupation is providing health care, or a trainee); health information or education; a social or leisure service within a health service; administration of a health service; writing a health status report (a report on your health prepared for another purpose, such as for an insurer, employer or court); relief of poverty, disadvantage, distress or hardship; emergency relief; care or protection of a child at risk; social advancement of disadvantaged groups; administration of a community service; employment search, placement or training; a housing service of the SA Housing Trust or a registered community housing provider; or none of these
      `I can have the housing decision reviewed by the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a housing service of the SA Housing Trust or a registered community housing provider: whether you can have its decision reviewed by the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal (directly or after an internal review)
GIVETH A `Service answer`
`Is my service one I can complain about` MEANS
    `the s 4 service answer for` `the kind of service` `with Tribunal review` `I can have the housing decision reviewed by the Tribunal`

@export Am I a person who may make a complaint to the South Australian Health and Community Services Complaints Commissioner about this service (s 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Complainant role` @desc Who you are: the consumer (the person who used, received or sought the service); a person the consumer appointed to complain for them; a parent or guardian of the consumer; the donee of the consumer's power of attorney (including a medical power of attorney); a substitute decision-maker under the consumer's advance care directive; a person acting for the consumer under another law or a court order; a Member of Parliament; another health or community service provider; a person who had an enduring relationship with the consumer; the consumer's personal representative (executor or administrator); or someone else
      `the consumer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The consumer's age in completed years (yours, if you are the consumer)
      `the consumer has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the consumer has died
      `the service was needed because of another provider's actions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are a provider: whether your complaint is that the service was or is provided, or was or is necessary, because of the actions of another provider
      `the Commissioner has approved me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, satisfied that it is unreasonable to expect the consumer to complain personally, has approved you to act for the consumer
GIVETH A `Standing answer`
`May I make this complaint` MEANS
    `the s 24 answer for` `my role` `age` `the consumer's age` `died` `the consumer has died` `provider ground` `the service was needed because of another provider's actions` `approved` `the Commissioner has approved me`

@export Is what I am complaining about a ground on which a complaint may be made under the South Australian Health and Community Services Complaints Act 2004 (s 25)?
GIVEN `what I allege` IS A `What the complaint alleges` @desc What the provider did: unreasonably did not provide, or stopped, a service; gave an unnecessary or inappropriate service; acted unreasonably in how it provided the service; failed to exercise due skill; failed to treat the consumer in a professional manner; failed to respect privacy or dignity; unreasonably failed to give enough information, choice, advice or prognosis; unreasonably denied or restricted access to the consumer's records; refused to hand over a copy of, or to change, medical records; unreasonably did not make information about the consumer's condition available; unreasonably disclosed information about the consumer to someone else; unreasonably did not deal properly with the consumer's own complaint to it; acted inconsistently with the Health and Community Services Rights Charter; fell short of the generally accepted standard of service; did not act or advise outside its own field of expertise; or something else
      `who received the information` IS A `Who received the information` @desc Only for a complaint about disclosure: who the information was disclosed to: a lawyer, in connection with a related legal matter; an insurer with an appropriate interest in the information; or another person
GIVETH A `Ground answer`
`Is this a ground I can complain on` MEANS
    `the s 25 answer for` `what I allege` `disclosed to` `who received the information`

@export The person I am complaining about was a volunteer: who is my complaint against, and can the volunteer be made to take part (s 25(5), (6))?
GIVEN `a volunteer did it while working for another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or omission was by a volunteer (someone unpaid for that role) while working for another person or body
      `a code of conduct applies to the volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a code of conduct prescribed under s 56A (the code for health care workers in Schedule 2 of the Regulations) applies to the volunteer
      `the Commissioner is satisfied of a risk to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the volunteer's conduct poses or has posed a risk to the health or safety of members of the public
GIVETH A `Volunteer answer`
`Who is my complaint about a volunteer against` MEANS
    `the s 25(5) answer for` `a volunteer did it while working for another` `code` `a code of conduct applies to the volunteer` `risk` `the Commissioner is satisfied of a risk to the public`

§§ `By when must I complain`

@export By when must I make my complaint to the South Australian Health and Community Services Complaints Commissioner, and was I in time (s 27)?
GIVEN `the day I first had notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you first had notice of the circumstances giving rise to the complaint
      `the day I might reasonably have had notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you might reasonably be expected to have had that notice (the same day, if you cannot say otherwise)
      `I have made the complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already made the complaint
      `the day I made it` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the complaint (any date, if not yet made)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `it is about a service to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint relates to a health or community service provided to a child (under 18)
      `the Commissioner has extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the time for your complaint
GIVETH A `Complaint time answer`
`By when must I complain` MEANS
    `the s 27 answer for notice on` `the day I first had notice` `or reasonably` `the day I might reasonably have had notice` `made` `I have made the complaint` `on` `the day I made it` `as of` `today` `child` `it is about a service to a child` `extended` `the Commissioner has extended my time`

@export Must I try to sort it out with the provider before my complaint can go ahead (s 29(5))?
GIVEN `I took reasonable steps with the provider first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took reasonable steps to resolve the matter with the provider before complaining (for example, raising it with the provider or its complaints officer)
      `I had good reason not to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a good reason for not doing so (for example, fear of reprisal, or the matter being too serious)
GIVETH A `First steps answer`
`Must I go to the provider first` MEANS
    `the s 29(5) answer for` `I took reasonable steps with the provider first` `good reason` `I had good reason not to`

§§ `Who deals with my complaint`

@export Will my complaint about a child protection service be sent to the Ombudsman (s 28A)?
GIVEN `the link to child protection` IS A `Child protection link` @desc What the service was: a service to or for a child who may be or has been at risk; a notification of a suspicion that a child may be at risk; an investigation of a case where a child may be at risk; a service to or for a child under the guardianship or in the custody of the Minister or another person under the Children and Young People (Safety) Act 2016; or none of these
      `it was provided by a government agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service was an administrative act of an agency to which the Ombudsman Act 1972 applies (in general, a State government department or agency, or a council)
      `it is in a class left with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is in a class that the published administrative arrangement between the Commissioner and the Ombudsman leaves with the Commissioner
GIVETH AN `Ombudsman answer`
`Will my child protection complaint go to the Ombudsman` MEANS
    `the s 28A answer for` `the link to child protection` `administrative act` `it was provided by a government agency` `arrangement` `it is in a class left with the Commissioner`

@export Who will deal with my complaint, given the kind of provider it is about (ss 29(3), 57)?
GIVEN `the provider` IS A `Kind of provider` @desc The provider complained about: a health practitioner registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (a doctor, nurse, dentist, pharmacist, psychologist, physiotherapist and the like); another provider registered under a South Australian law; an approved provider under the Aged Care Act 1997 of the Commonwealth (an aged care home or home care provider); or a provider that is not registered
GIVETH A `Handling answer`
`Who will deal with my complaint` MEANS
    `the handling answer for` `the provider`

§§ `While my complaint is dealt with`

@export The Commissioner asked me for more information, documents or a statutory declaration: was I in time, and what happens if I am late (ss 28, 33(1)(h))?
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner made the requirement
      `the last day I was given` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the Commissioner specified (or extended it to)
      `I have done it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have provided what was required
      `the day I did it` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided it (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `I had a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a good reason for not complying in time
GIVETH A `Requirement answer`
`Was I in time with the Commissioner's request` MEANS
    `the s 28 answer for a requirement on` `the day of the request` `ending` `the last day I was given` `met` `I have done it` `on` `the day I did it` `as of` `today` `good reason` `I had a good reason`

@export By when must the Commissioner decide what to do with my complaint, and is the decision overdue (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `the day the Commissioner received it` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner received your complaint
      `the days of delay allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of delay while the Commissioner or another person took steps required under the Act, or while the Commissioner made a preliminary inquiry (0 if none)
      `the Commissioner has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has made the determination (to conciliate, investigate, refer, or take no further action)
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the determination (any date, if none yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` MEANS
    `the s 29(1) answer for a complaint received on` `the day the Commissioner received it` `with delay` `the days of delay allowed` `determined` `the Commissioner has decided` `on` `the day of the decision` `as of` `today`

@export By when must the Commissioner tell me in writing what was decided on my complaint (s 29(6))?
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner made the determination on your complaint
      `I have been told in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received written notice of the determination
      `the day I was told` IS A DATE @desc The day the written notice was given (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`By when must I be told the decision on my complaint` MEANS
    `the s 29(6) answer for a determination on` `the day of the decision` `notified` `I have been told in writing` `on` `the day I was told` `as of` `today`

@export Can the Commissioner stop or suspend dealing with my complaint, for example because I have gone to court (s 33)?
GIVEN `a court or tribunal has decided all the issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all issues arising out of the subject matter have been adjudicated by a court, tribunal, authority or other body acting under an Australian law
      `court proceedings have begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings relating to the subject matter have been commenced in a court (for example, your claim for damages)
      `a coroner's inquest has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner has commenced an inquest relating to the subject matter
      `proceedings before another body have begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings relating to the subject matter have been commenced before a tribunal, authority or other body (for example, a registration board)
      `the ground the Commissioner relies on` IS A `Stopping ground` @desc Any other ground the Commissioner considers present: none; you are not entitled to complain; no ground of complaint is disclosed; it should be decided in legal proceedings; you have had reasonable explanations and there is no benefit in going on; you relied on a ground you should have disclosed at the start; it lacks substance or is frivolous, vexatious or not in good faith; you failed without good reason to comply or take a reasonable step; it would be an abuse of process; or it has been resolved or abandoned
GIVETH A `Stopping answer`
`Can the Commissioner stop dealing with my complaint` MEANS
    `the s 33 answer for` `a court or tribunal has decided all the issues` `court` `court proceedings have begun` `inquest` `a coroner's inquest has begun` `other proceedings` `proceedings before another body have begun` `ground` `the ground the Commissioner relies on`

@export If I withdraw my complaint, does everything stop (s 34)?
GIVEN `I gave written notice of withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Commissioner written notice withdrawing the complaint
      `the Commissioner is investigating a significant issue it raised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has determined to investigate a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance, or a significant question about a provider's practice, raised by the complaint (s 43(1)(c))
      `it was referred to another body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner referred the complaint to another person or body (such as a registration authority)
GIVETH A `Withdrawal answer`
`What happens if I withdraw my complaint` MEANS
    `the s 34 answer for` `I gave written notice of withdrawal` `s 43(1)(c)` `the Commissioner is investigating a significant issue it raised` `referred` `it was referred to another body`

§§ `Conciliation and informal mediation`

@export Can my complaint be resolved by conciliation or informal mediation (ss 29(4), 30(7), (8), 39(3), (4))?
GIVEN `it raises a significant public issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint appears to the Commissioner to indicate a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance
      `it raises a significant question about practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint appears to the Commissioner to indicate a significant question as to a provider's practice
GIVETH A `Conciliation answer`
`Can my complaint go to conciliation` MEANS
    `the conciliation answer for` `it raises a significant public issue` `practice` `it raises a significant question about practice`

@export Can someone help me, or represent me, at the conciliation (s 37)?
GIVEN `the help I want` IS A `Kind of help` @desc Whether the person would assist you or represent you (speak and act for you)
      `the conciliator has directed that person not act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conciliator has directed that that particular person not be allowed to act in the matter
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it would help substantially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that representation is likely to assist substantially in resolving the complaint
GIVETH A `Help answer`
`Can someone help me at conciliation` MEANS
    `the s 37 answer for` `the help I want` `direction` `the conciliator has directed that person not act` `satisfied` `the Commissioner is satisfied it would help substantially`

@export Can what was said in mediation or conciliation be used in my court case or other proceedings (ss 30(10), 40(1), 45(6))?
GIVEN `the process` IS A `Kind of process` @desc Where it was said or done: informal mediation during the Commissioner's preliminary inquiry; conciliation by a conciliator; or conciliation attempted during an investigation
      `it reveals a significant public issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it reveals a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the parties to the mediation or conciliation consent to its disclosure
GIVETH A `Disclosure answer`
`Can what was said in conciliation be used in court` MEANS
    `the disclosure answer for` `the process` `significant` `it reveals a significant public issue` `consent` `all the parties consent`

@export Is the agreement I reached with the provider in conciliation binding (s 42)?
GIVEN `it was reached in conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was reached in the course of the conciliation process
      `the day of the verbal agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day you and the provider agreed verbally in the conciliation
      `it has been put in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement has been entered into in writing
      `the day it was signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the written agreement was entered into (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Agreement answer`
`Is my conciliation agreement binding` MEANS
    `the s 42 answer for` `it was reached in conciliation` `verbal on` `the day of the verbal agreement` `written` `it has been put in writing` `on` `the day it was signed` `as of` `today`

§§ `After an investigation`

@export Will I get a copy of the Commissioner's report, notice or statement on my complaint (ss 54(2), 55(1)(b), (10), 56D(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of outcome document` @desc The document: the report of the investigation's findings and conclusions; a notice of recommended action to the provider; a report the Commissioner publishes after such a notice; or a statement of action taken against the provider under s 56C
      `it relates to my complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a s 56D statement: whether the action against the provider relates to your complaint
GIVETH A `Copy answer`
`Will I get a copy of the outcome` MEANS
    `the copy answer for` `the document` `relates` `it relates to my complaint`

@export Can the Commissioner stop the provider from providing health services (ss 56B, 56C, 56F; Regulations reg 8)?
GIVEN `it is a registration authority's matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct falls within Part 7 (complaints that the Commissioner deals with together with a registration authority, such as about a registered health practitioner's practice)
      `the stage of the investigation` IS AN `Investigation stage` @desc Whether the Commissioner has commenced, or has carried out (completed), an investigation of the provider, or neither
      `what the provider did` IS A `Provider conduct` @desc What the provider is said to have done: breached the code of conduct for health care workers (Regulations Schedule 2) that applies to them; an offence against the Australian Consumer Law (SA); an offence against Part 3 of the Criminal Law Consolidation Act 1935 (offences against the person); an offence against Part 7 Division 10 of the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (South Australia); an offence against the South Australian Public Health Act 2011; another offence; or none of these
      `the Commissioner reasonably believes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has a reasonable belief that the provider did it
      `the Commissioner is satisfied, or there is a conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the provider breached the code, or the provider has been found guilty of the offence
      `the Commissioner thinks action is needed to protect the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the Commissioner's opinion, action is necessary to protect the health or safety of members of the public
      `the Commissioner thinks the provider is an unacceptable risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the Commissioner's opinion, the provider poses an unacceptable risk to the health or safety of members of the public in providing health services
GIVETH AN `Order answer`
`Can the provider be stopped from practising` MEANS
    `the order answer for` `it is a registration authority's matter` `stage` `the stage of the investigation` `conduct` `what the provider did` `believes` `the Commissioner reasonably believes it` `satisfied or guilty` `the Commissioner is satisfied, or there is a conviction` `necessary` `the Commissioner thinks action is needed to protect the public` `unacceptable risk` `the Commissioner thinks the provider is an unacceptable risk`

§§ `My protection as a complainant`

@export Can the Commissioner keep my identity from the provider I complained about (s 74)?
GIVEN `disclosure would harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner believes on reasonable grounds that disclosing your identity would put someone's health or safety at risk, lead to a lower standard of service for someone, or prejudice the fair assessment of the complaint
      `it raises a significant public issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the Commissioner's opinion, the complaint raises a significant issue of public safety, interest or importance, or a significant question about a provider's practice
      `keeping it back is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the Commissioner's opinion, not disclosing your identity is in the public interest
GIVETH AN `Identity answer`
`Can my identity be kept from the provider` MEANS
    `the s 74 answer for` `disclosure would harm` `significant` `it raises a significant public issue` `public interest` `keeping it back is in the public interest`

@export Is it an offence for someone to threaten me, or to treat me badly, because I complained (ss 78, 79)?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What happened: threats or intimidation to stop you complaining, make you withdraw, stop you co-operating or giving information, or make you give false information; unfavourable treatment because you complained, co-operated or gave information (or were known or suspected to be about to); or something else
      `my complaint was a significant factor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For unfavourable treatment: whether your complaint, co-operation or information was at least a significant factor in why you were treated that way
      `I made a false allegation or acted in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For unfavourable treatment: whether the treatment was because you made a false allegation, or did not act in good faith
GIVETH A `Reprisal answer`
`Is it an offence to punish me for complaining` MEANS
    `the reprisal answer for` `what was done to me` `significant factor` `my complaint was a significant factor` `bad faith` `I made a false allegation or acted in bad faith`

@export Can the provider sue me for making my complaint (s 83)?
GIVEN `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the complaint, and gave any statements, information or documents, in good faith
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`Can I be sued for complaining` MEANS
    `the s 83 answer for` `I acted in good faith`
